Ostiole: a firewall and router appliance for Linux, with nftables underneath.

After installing the package run, as root:

    ostiole repair

It prints what it will do and asks: install the daemons a router needs,
write the units, hand addressing to systemd-networkd, remove the firewalls
and network managers it replaces, and start the web UI on https://<host>/.
Then create the admin account there and run the wizard.

Updates for a package install come from your package manager.
